---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Corrections & Updates — BrewTested"
  description="BrewTested corrections log. If you spot a factual error, outdated product, or wrong price, let us know."
>
  <article class="prose prose-amber max-w-none">
    <h1>Corrections & Updates</h1>
    <p>BrewTested is committed to factual accuracy. If you find an error — wrong ASIN, discontinued product, outdated price, inaccurate spec — report it and we will fix it.</p>

    <h2>How to Report an Error</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:paulet4a5@gmail.com">paulet4a5@gmail.com</a> with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The URL of the page with the error</li>
      <li>What is wrong and what the correct information is</li>
      <li>Source for the correct information (manufacturer page, Amazon listing, etc.)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We aim to correct factual errors within 48 hours of being notified.</p>

    <h2>Correction Policy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Factual errors (wrong specs, wrong ASINs, discontinued products) are corrected without notice</li>
      <li>Significant errors that affected recommendations are noted in page update history</li>
      <li>Corrections do not change original publication dates — we add "Last reviewed" dates to track updates</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Recent Updates</h2>
    <p>Updates are tracked on individual pages via the "Last reviewed" date. Major corrections are listed below.</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>May 2026:</strong> Updated OG image system to use dynamic Pollinations.ai portrait images (1000×1500) across all pages.</li>
      <li><strong>May 2026:</strong> Softened "café-quality" language across multiple pages — espresso machine descriptions now more accurately reflect research-based findings rather than subjective quality claims.</li>
      <li><strong>May 2026:</strong> Updated description fields from "We compared" to "Researched and ranked" to accurately reflect our research-based (not lab-test) methodology.</li>
      <li><strong>May 2026:</strong> Launched structured complaint index and espresso setup matrix as original research datasets.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Editorial Independence</h2>
    <p>Corrections are made based on accuracy, not commercial interests. A product's affiliate commission rate does not influence whether errors in its coverage are corrected or how they are corrected.</p>

    <p>For our full research methodology, see <a href="/methodology/">How BrewTested Researches Coffee Gear</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
